From b68936cfe70fb4728f81f05521ffe18076843ff0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Axel Tobieson <axel.tobieson@spiideo.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 22:44:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: port YUView internals analytics API +
 de265_internals_get_CB_QP
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ports the per-picture analytics API from the ChristianFeldmann/libde265
internal branch onto mainline v1.1.1:

- de265_internals.h / .cc: C-linkage externals for CTB slice indices,
  CB info (log2sz/partmode/predmode/PCM/transquant-bypass), PB motion
  vectors + refPOCs, intra direction (luma + chroma), TU flags, and new
  de265_internals_get_CB_QP (per min-CB QP_Y on the CB grid).
- de265_image: adds pixels_prediction/residual/tr_coeff + confwin
  counterparts, alloc_internals_planes() / release_internals_planes(),
  and the internals_get_* member functions that access the now-private
  metadata arrays directly.
- decoder_context: adds param_internals_save_prediction / _residual /
  _tr_coeff booleans; alloc_image hooks them to allocate extra planes.
- CMakeLists: adds de265_internals.cc to sources; de265_internals.h to
  public headers so it installs alongside de265.h.

Adaptation notes vs. the fork:
- No decctx-multilayer; casts to decoder_context* directly, same as
  de265.cc.
- Prediction/residual/tr_coeff planes are allocated (zero-filled) but
  not written by the decoder — mainline never saves the pre-SAO signal.
  The pointers are non-null and have correct stride; pixel data is all
  zeros. Writing the actual signals requires transform.cc/sao.cc hooks
  not present in mainline (out of scope for this port).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
